    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's more than just a critique though. it's a complete sanitization. the official papers make it look like everything just clicked into place, but the actual protocols for zero-centered initialization we used to bypass the stability bottleneck—the ones that kept the attention heads from diverging during the first 10k steps—well, they're nowhere to be found. it's like they wiped the slate clean so they could claim the architecture as a 'standard' discovery. i'm trying to see if i can even reconstruct the logic of those original safeguards from memory, because the math in the public docs just doesn't hold up to the actual training runs we did.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
